SUMMARY:Tom Sachs: Out and Back Run & Book Signing
DESCRIPTION:The Shop at PAM is proud to present a special event with Tom Sachs\, a 21st-century creative force whose critically acclaimed practice spans sculpture\, installation\, film\, and industrial design. \n\n\n\nJoin us for Tom’s signature event: the Out and Back run\, followed by an exclusive book signing. Rooted in movement and community\, the evening brings high energy to the Museum’s new West Plaza with happy-hour drinks and bites from the Shop at PAM and Coquelico. \n\n\n\nGet your Tom Sachs ISRU t-shirt for the run. Learn more about ISRU. \n\n\n\n\n5:30 p.m. – Out and Back mile run from the Museum through downtown\n\n\n\n6 – 7:30 p.m. – Book signing and happy hour\n\n\n\n\nAbout the book \n\n\n\n\n\nThe Tom Sachs Guide is the most comprehensive\, up-to-date look at Tom Sachs’s work\, documenting decades of rigorous and visionary artmaking. Vividly illustrated with more than 650 images and organized into thematic chapters\, the book includes work across mediums\, as well as long-standing collaborations with Nike and immersive reinterpretations of NASA missions. A rich appendix includes essential lists and charts\, offering insights into the artist’s creative process and studio practice. An object direct from the hands of the artist\, Tom Sachs Guide is a printed tour through his studio\, his body of work\, and the unique worlds he creates\, designed and written in close collaboration with Sachs himself. \n\n\n\nThe Tom Sachs Guide will be available in The Shop at PAM\, where visitors can find a delightful array of artistic offerings to deepen the experience of art and design at the Museum and around us.
URL:https://portlandartmuseum.org/event/tom-sachs-out-and-back-run-book-signing/
LOCATION:Portland Art Museum\, 1219 SW Park Ave\, Portland\, OR\, 97205
CATEGORIES:Free & discounted
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://portlandartmuseum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Tom-Sachs.jpg
END:VEVENT
