SUMMARY:But I'm a Cheerleader
DESCRIPTION:But I’m a Cheerleader (1999) Directed by Jamie Babbit. 1hr 25min. Rated R. \n\n\n\nGuest programmed by multidisciplinary artist and drag performer Pepper Pepper\, But I’m a Cheerleader (1999) is featured as part of our film series Pretty\, Witty and Gay—in conversation with the David Hockney exhibition. The queer romantic comedy cult classic satirizes “conversion therapy\,” suburbia\, and young love. \n\n\n\nWe do not generally provide advisories about subject matter or potentially triggering content in films\, and films exhibited don’t necessarily reflect the views of PAM CUT or the Portland Art Museum. In addition to the synopses\, trailers\, and other links on our website\, further information about content and age-appropriateness for specific films can be found on sites like Common Sense Media\, IMDb\, and DoesTheDogDie.com.
URL:https://portlandartmuseum.org/event/but-im-a-cheerleader/
